---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import cameras from '../../data/cameras.json';
import samples from '../../data/samples.json';
const rows=cameras.map(c=>({camera:c,sample:samples.find(s=>s.id===c.sampleId)!}));
---
<Layout title="Camera RAW File Sizes: Measured Samples & Chart" description="Compare measured RAW file sizes from Canon, Sony and Nikon camera samples. See how many RAW photos fit on a 128 GB card.">
<section class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">CAMERA FILE-SIZE INDEX</p><h1>Measured RAW file sizes by camera</h1><p>Compare original RAW files from three camera models. These are individual, verified sample-file sizes, not camera-wide averages. Compression mode, ISO and image content can change your results.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Original RAW sample measurements, decimal MB; 128 GB capacity is theoretical.</caption><thead><tr><th>Camera</th><th>RAW mode</th><th>File size</th><th>128 GB RAW photos</th><th>Original file</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(({camera,sample})=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/${sample.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`}>{camera.name}</a></th><td>{camera.modeLabel}</td><td>{(sample.rawBytes/1e6).toFixed(2)} MB</td><td>{Math.floor(128e9/sample.rawBytes).toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td><a href={sample.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">CC0 source ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>How are these numbers measured?</h2><p>We use the original RAW file byte counts recorded in our <a href="/methodology/">sample manifest and methodology</a>. One decimal megabyte equals 1,000,000 bytes. Card estimates divide the nominal decimal card capacity by the original file bytes, before filesystem overhead. JPEG storage estimates elsewhere on this site use an editable assumption, not measured standalone JPEG files.</p><h2>Find the right card capacity</h2><p>Open the <a href="/memory-card-calculator/">memory card calculator</a> to choose your camera, change file-size assumptions and compare RAW, JPEG or both. You can also <a href="/">compare RAW and JPEG renderings</a> side by side.</p></section>
</Layout>